Ticket #4471 is marked as one known issue. Its reports have more than one cause, so the queued
parser fix will not close all of them.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

- **`parser`:** the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get the day
  and month flipped. Tracked in [issue 1](https://github.com/jeremiasz-szczecina/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- **`hint`:** the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first, then reads the date day first.
  A parser fix does not change this. Tracked in [issue 2](https://github.com/jeremiasz-szczecina/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471's reports on the parser fix alone. Check the form reports from booking-v3 tenants separately.
</Callout>

## How to tell them apart

Use the tenant and the channel, not the subject line or the intake tag. The subject does not name
the cause, and intake guesses from the reporter's browser.

## Open question

The reports footnoted under the table describe a one-day move or a timing problem, not a day and
month flip. They stay under `parser` by the desk's rule. If they still reproduce after the parser
fix, they need their own ticket.

